# ==================================
# UniPlateTracker .dockerignore
# ==================================
#
# Without this file the build context is the entire working directory. On a
# machine that has run the app locally that is well over a gigabyte, almost
# all of it either rebuilt inside the image anyway or actively unwanted in it.

# --- Secrets ---
# The most important entries here. The builder stage does a COPY . . so
# anything matching would be readable inside that layer, and .env.local holds
# the PostgreSQL credentials and the DVLA API key. The image is built from
# source and takes its configuration at runtime; it must never carry a
# developer's environment file into the build.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Dependencies ---
# Reinstalled from the lockfiles by the deps stage. Copying a host node_modules
# in is both slow and wrong: native modules such as bcrypt are compiled for the
# host platform and will not necessarily run on Alpine.
node_modules
worker/node_modules

# --- Build output ---
# Regenerated by the builder stage. Copying a stale local build in risks it
# being picked up instead of the fresh one.
.next
out
worker/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Version control and CI ---
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Generated media ---
# Captures live on a mounted volume at runtime, never inside the image.
public/captures
worker/temp_segments

# --- Editor and agent state ---
.idea
.vscode
.claude
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# --- Local tooling and docs ---
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
README.md
LICENSE
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
*.pem
